! THE SECOND INDEX OF A VFL INSTRUCTION MODIFIES ITS OFFSET -- MCP's own
! octal conversion, run on the model.
!
! Reference Manual printed p.21 (PDF 24), read in the ink 2026-11-11:
!
!   "In the variable field instructions, the 19 bits which form the
!   length, byte size, and offset field are indexed as a single field.
!   Carries between parts of this field, if present, are not
!   suppressed."  "The index field I in the second half of the
!   instruction may be used to modify bits 35-50 of the instruction.
!   On doing this, bit position 3 of the index word is aligned with bit
!   position 35 of the instruction; the three high-order bits of the
!   index word are ignored."
!
! THE LOOP IS MCP'S.  Its JOB CONTROL BINARY LOADER converts an O card's
! six Hollerith digits this way (printed p.323 lines 46-50 and p.324
! lines 1-3, ALDADJ .. ALDA5): CT0011 sets the left-zeros count to the
! digit's row, LF(BU,3) moves its low three bits into the accumulator at
! the offset $2 gives, and $2 steps down by 1.32 -- three, in bits 3-18.
! From 30.32 the offsets are 61, 58, 55, 52, 49, 46, and SF(BU,18) at
! offset 46 takes the six digits.  Here the digits are 1 2 0 3 4 7, one
! column each, 12 bits, row 12 high (Appendix F), as on the card.
!
! FOUND BY THE LOADER, NOT BY READING: until 2026-11-11 the model decoded
! bits 60-63 into VflAddr.i2 and nothing read them, so every digit landed
! at offset 0 and the O card's origin came out zero -- TRIED TO LOAD
! OUTSIDE LIMITS on MCP's own loader (scratch probe of PUNREL stage 1).
!
! Checks: $3 (word 19) holds 120347 in its value field; $2 (word 18)
! ends at 21.32.  Not exercised: a carry across the length, byte-size
! and offset parts, and a negative index (the sign rule is CHOSEN in
! StretchExecute.bsv's vflSecondIndex).
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   LX,$1,DXW
        LVI,$2,30.32
LOOP    CT0011(BU,8)(V+I),.12($1)
        LF(BU,3),$LZC.4,($2)
        V-I,$2,1.32
        CB,$1,LOOP
        Z,$3
        SF(BU,18),$3,46
        BEW,$
        CNOP
        SLC, (8)400.0
DXW     XW,BUF.2,6
BUF     DD(BU,12),(8)0400                ! 1
        DD(BU,12),(8)0200                ! 2
        DD(BU,12),(8)1000                ! 0
        DD(BU,12),(8)0100                ! 3
        DD(BU,12),(8)0040                ! 4
        DD(BU,12),(8)0004                ! 7
        END,START
